WEBVTT

00:00:01.500 --> 00:00:17.435
<v Host>Welcome to Japanese Daily News. I'm Maya. Today is June fourteenth. In college baseball, the team from Kansai University won the national championship — their first title in fifty-four years. Let's listen.

00:00:18.036 --> 00:00:20.795
<v News>今日のニュースです。

00:00:21.495 --> 00:00:30.952
<v News>6月14日、大学野球の日本一を決める大会の決勝が、東京でありました。

00:00:31.652 --> 00:00:38.564
<v News>決勝では、関西大学と慶応大学が対戦しました。

00:00:39.264 --> 00:00:45.024
<v News>試合は、関西大学が2対1で勝ちました。

00:00:45.723 --> 00:00:52.636
<v News>関西大学の優勝は、54年ぶりで、3回目です。

00:00:53.335 --> 00:01:00.776
<v News>関西大学は、4回に1点を取って、先に点を取りました。

00:01:01.475 --> 00:01:08.603
<v News>5回には、山本選手がホームランを打って、点を増やしました。

00:01:09.304 --> 00:01:17.415
<v News>先発の米澤投手は、5回を投げて、相手に点を与えませんでした。

00:01:18.115 --> 00:01:26.852
<v News>慶応大学は、8回に1点を返しましたが、最後まで追いつけませんでした。

00:01:27.552 --> 00:01:34.103
<v News>優勝した選手たちは、グラウンドでとても喜んでいました。

00:01:34.804 --> 00:01:36.436
<v Host>Let's break it down.

00:01:37.036 --> 00:01:47.811
<v Slow>6月14日、大学野球の日本一を決める大会の決勝が、東京でありました。

00:01:48.611 --> 00:01:56.075
<v Host>On June fourteenth, the final of the tournament that decides Japan's best college baseball team was held in Tokyo.

00:01:56.676 --> 00:01:59.028
<v Vocab>決勝

00:01:59.427 --> 00:02:07.828
<v Host>It means the final — the last game that decides the winner. The first character means to decide, the second means victory.

00:02:08.427 --> 00:02:16.324
<v Slow>決勝では、関西大学と慶応大学が対戦しました。

00:02:17.123 --> 00:02:21.707
<v Host>In the final, Kansai University faced Keio University.

00:02:22.307 --> 00:02:24.587
<v Vocab>対戦

00:02:24.987 --> 00:02:31.972
<v Host>It means to face off, to compete against. You'll hear it for any match between two teams or players.

00:02:32.572 --> 00:02:39.147
<v Slow>試合は、関西大学が2対1で勝ちました。

00:02:39.948 --> 00:02:43.955
<v Host>In the game, Kansai University won, two to one.

00:02:44.556 --> 00:02:46.788
<v Vocab>試合

00:02:47.187 --> 00:02:53.163
<v Host>It means a game or a match. This is the everyday word for any sports contest.

00:02:53.764 --> 00:03:01.659
<v Slow>関西大学の優勝は、54年ぶりで、3回目です。

00:03:02.460 --> 00:03:08.580
<v Host>It was Kansai University's first championship in fifty-four years, and their third overall.

00:03:09.180 --> 00:03:11.532
<v Vocab>優勝

00:03:11.931 --> 00:03:19.348
<v Host>It means winning the championship — finishing first. The word literally combines being superior with victory.

00:03:19.948 --> 00:03:28.467
<v Slow>関西大学は、4回に1点を取って、先に点を取りました。

00:03:29.268 --> 00:03:33.924
<v Host>Kansai University took one point in the fourth inning, scoring first.

00:03:34.524 --> 00:03:36.348
<v Vocab>点

00:03:36.747 --> 00:03:43.635
<v Host>It means a point, or a score. To take a point is to score; you'll hear it in every sports report.

00:03:44.235 --> 00:03:52.372
<v Slow>5回には、山本選手がホームランを打って、点を増やしました。

00:03:53.171 --> 00:03:58.187
<v Host>In the fifth inning, player Yamamoto hit a home run, adding to the score.

00:03:58.788 --> 00:04:01.044
<v Vocab>選手

00:04:01.443 --> 00:04:09.436
<v Host>It means an athlete or a player. Add it after a name or sport to mean that player — useful all over sports news.

00:04:10.036 --> 00:04:19.324
<v Slow>先発の米澤投手は、5回を投げて、相手に点を与えませんでした。

00:04:20.124 --> 00:04:26.267
<v Host>The starting pitcher, Yonezawa, pitched five innings and gave up no points to the other team.

00:04:26.867 --> 00:04:29.100
<v Vocab>投手

00:04:29.500 --> 00:04:35.932
<v Host>It means pitcher — the player who throws the ball in baseball. The first character means to throw.

00:04:36.531 --> 00:04:46.516
<v Slow>慶応大学は、8回に1点を返しましたが、最後まで追いつけませんでした。

00:04:47.315 --> 00:04:52.884
<v Host>Keio University got one point back in the eighth inning, but couldn't catch up in the end.

00:04:53.483 --> 00:04:55.788
<v Vocab>追いつく

00:04:56.187 --> 00:05:03.004
<v Host>It means to catch up, to draw level. Here, the team that was behind couldn't quite reach the other's score.

00:05:03.603 --> 00:05:06.603
<v Host>Let's listen to the full story one more time.

00:05:07.204 --> 00:05:09.963
<v News>今日のニュースです。

